    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d116-a1">

                <pb facs="0208" n="942" xml:id="pg942"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Governor McIntire to
                        Mr. Gresham</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Denver, Colo.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-03-16"><hi rendition="#italic">March 16,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have reliable information that two of the Italians lynched positively had first
                    and probably second citizenship papers. Not known whether Danino was an American
                    citizen. It is asserted that the two prisoners who may have escaped from first
                    attack of mob had first citizenship papers. The fate of the last two not known,
                    as they have not been heard from since their escape. I have directed proper
                    district attorney to take speedy steps looking to arrest and conviction of the
                    guilty parties in the Walsenburg affair.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Albert W. McIntire</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Governor</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
